== Temporal Validation Across Independent Collection Dates

A major vulnerability in machine learning evaluations is sensitivity to temporal environmental drift and collection artifacts. In operational enterprise environments, Active Directory graphs mutate continuously as users log on, temporary sessions expire, and security groups are modified.

To establish whether CertGraph maintains stable representations over time, we conducted three independent data collections against the running GOAD virtual machines across distinct calendar dates:

+ *Collection Baseline (T1):* June 15, 2026.
+ *Follow-up Snapshot (T2):* July 2, 2026 (17 days later, following intermediate red-team simulation exercises).
+ *Validation Snapshot (T3):* August 10, 2026 (56 days later, following system patching and host reboots).



CertGraph (trained exclusively on synthetic data) was evaluated zero-shot against all three temporal snapshots without fine-tuning:

+ `sevenkingdoms.local`: $7 / 7$ test cases correctly classified across all dates ($100.0%$).
+ `north.sevenkingdoms.local`: $7 / 7$ test cases correctly classified across all dates ($100.0%$).
+ `essos.local`: $7 / 7$ test cases correctly classified across all dates ($100.0%$).
+ *Aggregate Temporal Accuracy:* $bold(63 / 63)$ test cases correctly classified ($bold(100.0%)$).


This multi-week temporal validation confirms that CertGraph's learned relational representations are invariant to transient session noise and background administrative churn.

== External Community Benchmark Validation

To eliminate dataset collection bias and verify model robustness on telemetry collected outside our local virtualization lab, we evaluated CertGraph against an independent open-source enterprise dataset from the `m4lwhere/Bloodhound-CE-Sample-Data` repository. This repository contains raw SharpHound telemetry collected from an external, multi-domain GOADv2 installation managed by independent security researchers.

