As shown in @tab:community_results, across 30 test scenarios spanning the three external enterprise domains, CertGraph maintained a perfect *100.0% accuracy*, whereas signature-based heuristics averaged only *63.3%*. The performance gain of $+36.7%$ was driven by CertGraph's ability to discover relational vectors (such as ESC13) and suppress false positives on hardened templates. This validates that CertGraph's relational representations transfer seamlessly across independent enterprise directory collections.
